1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,600
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:24,217
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,917
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:10,117
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real.

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,077
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:24,277
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:28,237
So come aboard and bring along.

24
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:30,560
All your hopes and dreams.

25
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,877
Together we will find everything.

26
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:35,960
That we're looking for.

27
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you.

28
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,420
If you wanna be my friend.

29
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,820
We are, we are on a cruise.

30
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,700
We are.

31
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,030
What's wrong?

32
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:56,817
The mayor's never been
gone for this long before.

33
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,837
I hope he's all right.

34
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:00,257
It sounded like a battle
was going on in town.

35
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:03,458
There's been a lot more
cannon fire than usual today.

36
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,737
I'll go to town to check it out.

37
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,220
You all just stay here.

38
00:02:07,380 --> 00:02:09,340
I'm going with you. No way.

39
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,417
There are still pirates in town.

40
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:13,500
It's too dangerous of a situation.

41
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:14,450
Yes, exactly.

42
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,977
That's why you'll need our help.

43
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:18,257
What kind of citizens
are we if we don't help?

44
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,617
We have got to find out what's happening.

45
00:02:20,700 --> 00:02:22,357
You can't stop us from going.

46
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:24,616
We want to do all we can to help out.

47
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,180
Then it's settled.

48
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,960
We all go together.

49
00:02:35,440 --> 00:02:40,160
In all my life, I've never
been as mad at someone as him.

50
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,860
That bastard Shank stole
countless riches from me.

51
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:48,917
I don't know how you two are connected,
but I can say whatever I want about him.

52
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,300
I've earned that!

53
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:58,400
The North Pole! South Pole!

54
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,756
That's what you say!

55
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:02,837
Right, and I'm gonna keep on
saying it because I'm right, clown!

56
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,120
Oh, you got guts?

57
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:06,137
I'm gonna settle this once and for all!

58
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:07,220
Go ahead and try!

59
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:10,537
All right, you bastard, I'm
gonna bust you up flashily!

60
00:03:10,620 --> 00:03:11,450
Counterattack!

61
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:12,363
Knock it off!

62
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:16,177
Nobody but you two cares which is
colder, the North Pole or the South.

63
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:19,897
If you want to know so badly, then
why don't you go to both and find out?

64
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:20,810
Now call it.

65
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:21,970
The ship!

66
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:28,540
Enemy ship to the north-north-east!
Right. Get ready. Time to fight.

67
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,560
Yes, sir!

68
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:30,990
Yes.

69
00:03:31,073 --> 00:03:32,217
I can't wait to plunder.

70
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:34,520
You seem happy, Buggy. Obviously.

71
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,737
Enemy ships are just like
big floating treasure chests.

72
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:39,877
It's only natural for
pirates to raid them.

73
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:40,790
Am I wrong?

74
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,037
Well, there's some truth to that.

75
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,017
You're too weak.

76
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,657
You and everyone else here
just don't have the pirate's

77
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:49,357
natural hunger and desire
for plundering treasure.

78
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:52,028
You don't know what it
means to be a pirate.

79
00:03:59,460 --> 00:04:00,320
What's this?

80
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,430
It's...

81
00:04:02,513 --> 00:04:03,343
huh?

82
00:04:03,426 --> 00:04:04,256
Treasure map.

83
00:04:04,339 --> 00:04:05,700
I've never seen one before.

84
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:06,881
It's incredible.

85
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,969
Is the treasure at the
bottom of the ocean?

86
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:13,010
Yes.

87
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:17,540
Now my life's path is flashily decided!

88
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,240
Hey, Buggy!

89
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,277
Aren't you gonna come celebrate with us?

90
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:37,237
We've found a whole lot
of really neat stuff!

91
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,150
It's no map!

92
00:04:38,233 --> 00:04:40,660
I don't have anything hidden! Go away!

93
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,757
What are you talking about, Buggy?

94
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,060
Oh, uh, nothing.

95
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:50,757
You said you were gonna leave
this ship sometime, right?

96
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,000
So, what do you plan to do?

97
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:58,080
I'm gonna get my own ship, then gather
a reliable crew and see the world.

98
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,860
I'm gonna take my time.

99
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,084
Ha, all as a pirate, of course.

100
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:06,840
What a bunch of sentimental
nonsense! Say what?

101
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:09,413
I do admire your fighting skill, though.

102
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:13,840
If you weren't such a softy,
I'd make you one of my henchmen.

103
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,080
Your henchmen?

104
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,200
I don't think so. Huh?

105
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,717
We have completely
different outlooks on life,

106
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:22,997
so I think we should just
follow our own paths.

107
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,433
That's what pirates do.

108
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:29,177
You think you're such an expert on
pirates, but if we ever meet on the ocean,

109
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:31,848
then we'd have to have
a fight to the death.

110
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,780
Yeah, pirates do that too.

111
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,820
You never make sense.

112
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:40,937
Anyways, you said something about
finding some interesting loot, right?

113
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:41,850
Huh?

114
00:05:41,933 --> 00:05:43,097
Oh yeah, we found a Devil Fruit.

115
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,010
A Devil Fruit?

116
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:47,917
I heard that the different fruits
are incarnations of the sea devil.

117
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,117
Supposedly, if you eat
one, you gain devil powers,

118
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:53,494
but the sea will hate you and
take your ability to swim.

119
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:56,131
You'd have to be stupid to eat that thing.

120
00:05:57,040 --> 00:06:00,922
I'd never get that treasure on the
ocean floor if I couldn't swim.

121
00:06:01,540 --> 00:06:06,760
But still, I bet you could sell that fruit
for at least a hundred million berries.

122
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:09,970
What?!

123
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:14,700
I, Pirate Apprentice Buggy, am
about to devour this Devil Fruit!

124
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:17,820
You gotta love the kids!

125
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,824
Never thinking of consequences!

126
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,620
Well, Buggy?

127
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,526
You feel any differently yet?

128
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,557
No, not really.

129
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:31,020
Aw, was it a fake?

130
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:32,880
I'm not surprised.

131
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,471
I've never seen a real Devil Fruit before.

132
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:40,460
Yes, that worked flashily well.

133
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:45,807
These guys are so gullible, I can't
believe I was able to trick them so easily.

134
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:49,604
Now to jump ship before
they find out the truth.

135
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:53,377
With the money I get from selling this
Devil Fruit and finding the sunken treasure,

136
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:55,813
I'll easily be able to form my own crew.

137
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:57,437
Hey there, Rocky.

138
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,344
Were you just saying something?

139
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,510
Oh, you!

140
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,997
Don't scare me like that!

141
00:07:02,080 --> 00:07:03,240
Don't be so jumpy.

142
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:06,437
And don't steal too much
food from the kitchen.

143
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,417
You don't want to make the cook mad.

144
00:07:08,500 --> 00:07:09,580
That was close.

145
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:11,570
Oh, yeah!

146
00:07:11,653 --> 00:07:13,342
The captain told me to tell you.

147
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:22,760
Hey, what's wrong? Bastard! Why? Why? Why?

148
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:26,248
What's that piece of paper?

149
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:27,920
Not my map!

150
00:07:28,980 --> 00:07:30,040
Hey buggy

151
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,660
What what's going on?

152
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:35,500
I can't move

153
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:40,280
Is it true that you lose
your ability to swim damn it?

154
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:43,380
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

155
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:44,800
What's going on?

156
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,412
Why aren't you swimming?

157
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:48,790
Buggy

158
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:54,097
I'll save you.

159
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:55,010
Buggy

160
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,937
So, are you telling me
that Shank saved your life?

161
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:10,337
Yo, that's not the point
I'm trying to get across!

162
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:11,757
Because of what he did to me,

163
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:15,477
I was unable to swim and therefore
unable to obtain my sunken treasure!

164
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,972
Then I had a revelation.

165
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:21,477
If I couldn't go underwater, then I'd
just obtain all the treasure on dry land.

166
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:24,200
Using my brand new Chop Chop powers.

167
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:27,717
And now, I won't let anyone
who touches my treasure live.

168
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:31,447
Death to those who tried to build
for my hard-earned treasure!

169
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,060
Get back here, you thief!

170
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:39,880
Damn it!

171
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:40,980
He spotted me!

172
00:08:42,420 --> 00:08:45,760
You don't stand a chance
of escaping from me! Now!

173
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,280
I'm going to flashily chop you off!

174
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:06,720
Ow, my balls, my balls,
that was a cheap shot.

175
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,320
Don't run off yet, we're not done.

176
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,977
Hey, you better drop that treasure
and get out of here, Nami.

177
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:16,277
You don't want him coming after you again.

178
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,340
No, drop the money and go?

179
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:21,426
No way, why should I
leave my treasure behind?

180
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,300
Did you just call it your treasure?

181
00:09:25,660 --> 00:09:26,797
That's right, you heard me.

182
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,957
I'm a thief who steals from pirates,

183
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:32,117
and I just stole a lot of treasure
from a really annoying one.

184
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:34,965
So that makes this my
treasure now, understand?

185
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:38,060
Ah, that makes sense.

186
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:39,840
That's pure nonsense!

187
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:43,257
That's my treasure, and just because you
stole it from me doesn't make it yours,

188
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:44,752
you dirty, sneaky thief!

189
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:47,820
Honestly, what did your parents teach you?

190
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:51,917
A criminal trying to
lecture another criminal?

191
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,640
Ridiculous. What's that?

192
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:54,990
Whatever.

193
00:09:55,073 --> 00:09:59,033
The day I take a morality lesson from
you is the day I stop being a thief.

194
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,532
I hope you're ready for the consequences.

195
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:10,020
Now, here comes Chop Chop Festival!

196
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:20,000
I'd like to see you try and save your
friend for me now, Gum-Gum! Damn it!

197
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,300
He broke up into smaller pieces!

198
00:10:24,660 --> 00:10:25,857
What the...

199
00:10:25,940 --> 00:10:26,780
Nami!

200
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,160
Give me back my treasure! No way!

201
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:42,240
See how you like this?

202
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:46,060
Dammit! Knock it off!

203
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,480
No, you knock it off!

204
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:58,080
Thanks for giving me
my treasure back, Nami.

205
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:01,280
Don't let go! You let go!

206
00:11:01,420 --> 00:11:04,217
This is my treasure, so get
your grubby hands off him!

207
00:11:04,300 --> 00:11:06,065
Just give me back my treasure!

208
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:09,870
Die!

209
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:13,317
I already told you!

210
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,812
You haven't finished dealing with me yet!

211
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:46,182
Consider that finishing move a
little gift from the old mayor guy.

212
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:48,300
Thanks a lot.

213
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:49,520
I owe you one.

214
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,880
Sure, no problem.

215
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:53,120
Oh yeah, the map!

216
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,900
This isn't over yet, Gum-Gum!

217
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:59,980
He's still alive! Shut up!

218
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,060
How dare you flashily do this to me!

219
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,640
You'll pay for this!

220
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:08,880
Assemble, Chop Chop Pods!

221
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,710
Huh?

222
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:23,460
Who looking for these, Buggy? Gah!

223
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:24,800
My box!

224
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,230
Ha ha ha ha!

225
00:12:26,313 --> 00:12:28,040
All right! Here you go, B!

226
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,880
Stop it now!

227
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:31,660
See ya, Buggy!

228
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:33,660
Now come go!

229
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,880
Let's go go!

230
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:49,840
I win!

231
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:53,610
Whoa!

232
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:56,140
That kid sure's Captain Buggy flying!

233
00:12:56,340 --> 00:12:58,869
So, what do we do
without the captain, huh?

234
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:01,540
Keep acting unconscious. Good idea.

235
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,826
Sorry your hat's all torn up.

236
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,550
Don't worry.

237
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:11,877
I can still put it on.

238
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:15,136
And I got Buggy out of here,
so I'm satisfied for now.

239
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:17,770
Bastard!

240
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:22,720
When I have time, I'll fix
it for you, if you like

241
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:24,210
What's that?

242
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,170
Oh, forget it.

243
00:13:25,253 --> 00:13:28,757
I split this into two bags, so give
me a hand and carry half of it.

244
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,520
It's too heavy for me.

245
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:32,417
That sure is a lot.

246
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:36,077
If anything, that clown buggy knew
quality treasure when he saw it,

247
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,117
and now it's all mine.

248
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:40,376
I bet I can sell this for
at least 10 million berries.

249
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:47,180
Here you go. Huh?

250
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:49,097
It's the chart to the Grand Line.

251
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:50,617
You do want it, don't you?

252
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:51,697
You're giving it to me?

253
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:53,309
Because you saved my life.

254
00:13:55,500 --> 00:13:56,460
Thanks, Nami!

255
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,500
Now I finally have it!

256
00:13:58,620 --> 00:14:00,557
A map of the Grand Line! Hooray!

257
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:03,577
Oh, does this also mean you'll
be joining me and my pirate crew?

258
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:07,072
I told you, no matter what,
I'll never join a pirate crew!

259
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:11,957
But okay, hanging around with
you seems profitable enough.

260
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:16,120
Just remember this, I'm only joining
you because it's in my interest.

261
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:17,550
Sure.

262
00:14:20,180 --> 00:14:21,800
Hey, Zoro, wake up.

263
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,340
Zoro, we're leaving.

264
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,817
Do we take care of everything?

265
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:31,841
Yeah, and we got a navigator, and
we got a chart of the Grand Line.

266
00:14:36,360 --> 00:14:38,000
I'm not sure about this.

267
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,318
I feel lightheaded.

268
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:40,620
Of course you do.

269
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,527
It's always something
with you two, honestly.

270
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:44,717
Hey, wait a minute.

271
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:45,630
What did I do?

272
00:14:45,713 --> 00:14:46,543
Are you kidding me?

273
00:14:46,626 --> 00:14:47,877
You're the worst of them all!

274
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,901
Anyways, let's go help the mayor.

275
00:14:50,480 --> 00:14:51,310
Oh, yeah.

276
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:55,037
I guess we should wake the old
guy up now that it's all over.

277
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,950
You there!

278
00:14:56,033 --> 00:14:59,360
You're not residents of this
village? Nope. And who are you?

279
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,997
What was all that cannon fire we heard?

280
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:05,337
It sounded like there may have
been a battle here earlier.

281
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:07,596
If you know anything, please tell us.

282
00:15:08,060 --> 00:15:08,890
Oh, good.

283
00:15:08,973 --> 00:15:09,803
They're just citizens.

284
00:15:09,886 --> 00:15:12,137
I thought that maybe
they were more pirates.

285
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:15,637
Oh, mayor! Oh, no! Say
something! Can you hear me?

286
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:20,537
He's out cold the pirates
definitely did this how horrible no,

287
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:23,120
I'm the one who kicked that old man's ass

288
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:27,957
Hold on you didn't have to tell
them that did you it's true.

289
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,334
Maybe you should explain to
them so they don't get angry

290
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,877
Tell me why exactly did you
knock our mayor out and leave him

291
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,977
in the street to die better
explain yourselves who are you?

292
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:40,531
Are you with the pirates?

293
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:43,778
They're getting really bloodthirsty.

294
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:46,597
We can't let them know that
we're thieves and pirates.

295
00:15:46,680 --> 00:15:47,600
We're pirates.

296
00:15:51,260 --> 00:15:52,640
Just as we thought.

297
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,560
It's the truth.

298
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:58,640
Pirates, how dare you ravage our town.

299
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:02,142
We won't show you any
mercy for what you've done.

300
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:03,530
What now?

301
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:06,386
Doesn't look like they're
up for a discussion.

302
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:08,290
Run!

303
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:16,120
How dare you hurt a beloved mayor!

304
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,540
How do you always make things worse?

305
00:16:23,860 --> 00:16:25,380
This is a good town. Huh?

306
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:29,259
Everyone's so mad just
because of the old mayor guy.

307
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:38,097
Something tells me they're not gonna
listen to our side of the story.

308
00:16:38,180 --> 00:16:39,117
We're turning here.

309
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:40,030
Huh?

310
00:16:40,113 --> 00:16:41,060
Wait, hold on!

311
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,497
You gotta let me know sooner!

312
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:43,992
They ran into the alley!

313
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:51,040
Chouchou? Doggy?

314
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,540
Hey, move!

315
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,212
Chouchou, get out of here!

316
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,160
Those three are pirates!

317
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:02,758
They're barking at the wrong people!

318
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:05,717
Why isn't he letting us pass through?

319
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,920
Chouchou, get out of here! Woof! Woof!

320
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:09,940
Later, doggy!

321
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:22,000
That was close.

322
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:24,520
We only made it because of Chouchou.

323
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,937
Why do we have to put up with this?

324
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:28,017
Does it matter now?

325
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,437
We're done here anyway.

326
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:31,437
Yeah, maybe so, but...

327
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:32,873
Hey, is this your boat?

328
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,280
It's great!

329
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:37,157
It's nothing special,
but I guess it'll do.

330
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,917
I stole it from some dumb
pirates a few days back.

331
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,588
That's a big mouth you got.

332
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:45,117
We've been waiting for
you, you little thief.

333
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:48,553
Never thought you'd run into
us here, now did you, girly?

334
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,136
You know these guys?

335
00:17:51,380 --> 00:17:52,737
Yeah, sort of.

336
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,397
Hey, it's not just sort of.

337
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:56,157
We're bound together by fate.

338
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,677
So these are your friends.

339
00:17:57,760 --> 00:18:00,337
I guess we'll have to punish
the two of them as well.

340
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:04,479
It's time you learn what happens
when you steal other people's stuff.

341
00:18:04,600 --> 00:18:05,430
Hey, you.

342
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:06,650
You hear me?

343
00:18:06,733 --> 00:18:08,287
Take time for your medicine!

344
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,360
Hey, look!

345
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:21,920
He's waking up!

346
00:18:24,160 --> 00:18:25,680
Thank goodness he's fine.

347
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:27,509
What happened here, Mayor?

348
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:31,457
What in the...

349
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,540
It was like this when we got here.

350
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:37,626
There were a few pirates when we
arrived, but they all ran off.

351
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:40,585
Can you tell us what happened?

352
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:43,780
Where are the young ones? What's that?

353
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:46,494
Are you talking about those three kids?

354
00:18:46,820 --> 00:18:48,620
So they're still alive?

355
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:53,680
Those fools, treating a
senior citizen like that.

356
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:54,800
How rude.

357
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:58,737
We drove those pirates out of town, Mayor.

358
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:00,297
You don't have to worry
about them anymore.

359
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:01,680
But it's not enough.

360
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:04,757
We have to make them pay for
what they've done to our village

361
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,737
They deserve to be punished for
destroying the peaceful town.

362
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,297
We all worked so hard to build.

363
00:19:09,380 --> 00:19:10,480
Yeah, she's right

364
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:14,493
There's still time to go after
them if we hold your mouth

365
00:19:14,840 --> 00:19:17,857
I'm the only one who's allowed
to complain about those kids.

366
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:21,560
I won't let anyone else
badmouth them You hear me? What?

367
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,177
Why are you protecting
those pirates mayor?

368
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,090
Damn it?

369
00:19:25,173 --> 00:19:27,437
They think they can just
disappear and that's that

370
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:28,717
Where did they go?

371
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,417
Well I think they were running toward the

372
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:37,260
port Damn kids they can't
just leave like that

373
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:41,940
I have a lot of things
I want to say to you all

374
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:50,537
All right let's get going can
I ask you something Isn't that

375
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:54,217
Buggy's mark on your sail well this
This did used to be Buggy's boat.

376
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,771
Think I should change it?

377
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,570
Hey, wait!

378
00:19:59,653 --> 00:20:00,720
Young ones!

379
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,660
It's the old mayor guy.

380
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,097
I was ready to die.

381
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:16,200
I was ready to die filled with despair.

382
00:20:19,020 --> 00:20:20,640
Thanks! Thank you!

383
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:25,940
Don't worry about it!

384
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,200
Take it easy!

385
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:30,817
Damn you, young ones.

386
00:20:30,900 --> 00:20:32,377
Damn you, young ones.

387
00:20:32,460 --> 00:20:34,020
Damn you, young ones.

388
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,600
I have no words.

389
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,677
What'd you do, Luffy?!

390
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:48,617
Don't tell me you left that
bag of treasure back there!

391
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:49,530
Yeah!

392
00:20:49,613 --> 00:20:51,637
That bag was worth around five
million berries, you idiot!

393
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,560
That's right,

394
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,537
and they're gonna need
that money to repair

395
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:57,097
their destroyed town But
that was my treasure,

396
00:20:57,180 --> 00:20:58,010
jerk!

397
00:20:58,093 --> 00:21:00,311
Do you know how hard I worked to steal it?

398
00:21:01,220 --> 00:21:02,840
Why didn't you do that?

399
00:21:03,140 --> 00:21:04,400
No, I can't swim!

400
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:06,134
That's the whole idea!

401
00:21:06,440 --> 00:21:08,697
If you want it, just go
back and get it then!

402
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:09,817
I can't do that!

403
00:21:09,900 --> 00:21:11,140
You go get it! No!

404
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:12,540
That's dangerous!

405
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,896
I can die, you know!

406
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:14,900
I don't care!

407
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:18,886
And if you do that again, I really
will throw you in the ocean!

408
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:25,304
Well, for better or for worse, looks like
we finally have a navigator in our crew.

409
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:50,037
My way to that place.

410
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:52,897
Before someone could beat me.

411
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:57,097
The promised land was in my grasp.

412
00:21:57,180 --> 00:21:59,640
And I wouldn't let go.

413
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:03,557
La la la la.

414
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:04,917
My only dream.

415
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,160
La la la la la.

416
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:12,840
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true.

417
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:21,437
But if the world ever
changes, I call out your name.

418
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:28,060
We could return to the time
when everything's the same.

419
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:35,297
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

420
00:22:35,380 --> 00:22:40,660
Waiting for that one true dream. You?
